Ah, well, maybe I don't deserve to win this game.  After having the
most wonderful time in my career as a nethack addict, I had become the
Most Dangerous Dude in the Dungeon.  Hell had gotten boring.  I lost
track of how many times I had killed the Wizard.  I Dis'ed the
Invisible Dispatcher.  I licked the Lichs.  Dragons, Purple Worms,
Minotaurs: they were all chumps.  I was just looking for that !@#$%^&*
amulet and a level teleport trap to get me out of this.

So what happened?  Well, I came across one those funny little rooms in
the center, see, and I wanted to cross the moat to get to the other
side.  I put on the ring, crossed over, took off the ring, no problem.
I slaughtered the invisible dispatcher, and (oh brother) here comes
that pesky Evoker of Yendor again, so I butcher him, too.  That was all
yesterday.  I saved the game, got on with my life and resumed today.
Stupidly I did not review the contents of my pack upon restart.  Just
as stupidly, I didn't just decide to teleport across the moat.  Put on
what?--More--a cursed ring of levitation (on left hand).

The rest was somewhat inevitable.

I had already identified the uncursed ring of polymorph I was carrying,
so I removed all my armor and put the polymorph ring on my right hand
and waited to polymorph into something with no ring fingers.  Soon I
got too weak to teleport, and shortly after that I was set upon by more
monsters than I could handle naked.

Stupid, stupid, stupid...

